# Railway — always redeploy after main

Production: `https://regenold-eu-ai-act-rag-production.up.railway.app`

## Policy

Whenever code that affects production is **merged or pushed to `main`**, ensure Railway deploys the latest commit. Do not assume a silent auto-deploy happened.

## Preferred path (CI)

- Push to `main` runs `.github/workflows/railway-redeploy.yml` (`railway redeploy --yes --from-source`).
- Requires GitHub repo secrets: `RAILWAY_TOKEN` (required), optional `RAILWAY_SERVICE_ID`, `RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT`, `RAILWAY_PROJECT_ID`.
- Setup: `docs/partners/regenold/RAILWAY_DEPLOY.md`.

## Manual / local path

From repo root (Windows):

```powershell
$env:RAILWAY_TOKEN = "<token from railway.com account tokens>"
.\scripts\redeploy-railway.ps1
```

Or: `npx @railway/cli redeploy --yes --from-source` after `railway link` or with `-p` / `-s` / `-e` flags.

## Verify after deploy

```powershell
curl https://regenold-eu-ai-act-rag-production.up.railway.app/healthz
curl https://regenold-eu-ai-act-rag-production.up.railway.app/healthz/llm
```

## Agent checklist (end of ship PR)

1. Merge/push to `main`.
2. Confirm GitHub Actions **Redeploy Railway production** succeeded (or run `scripts/redeploy-railway.ps1`).
3. Probe `/healthz` and spot-check `/api/v1/regenold/eu-ai-act/ask` if behaviour changed.
